<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Armenian Oblast</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1828">1828</a>–<a href="/years/1840">1840</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Armenian Oblast was a province of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> formed in 1828 from the Erivan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nakhchivan">Nakhichevan</a> khanates ceded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-turkmenchay">Treaty of Turkmenchay</a>. Many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenians">Armenians</a> from Iran resettled there. It was abolished in 1840 and its lands were later reorganised as the Erivan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/governorate">Governorate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/armenian-oblast.jpg" alt="Armenian Oblast" width="320" height="435" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Brindz · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Armyanskaya_Oblast.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
